{"about":"9843f16c55a02ce422d04eb9057d52cb554dfe0052e19a3d19653ba96e18dc92","body":"The conjecture forbids claiming that selecting a highly corroborated theory provides any rational basis for believing it is true or approximately true; it must strictly maintain that such selection offers no epistemic justification beyond the report of past survival, accepting the cost that science cannot claim progressive approach to truth without smuggling in induction.","kind":"mini.commitment-proposal.v1","named":"The cost of abandoning epistemic justification"}